+Stops entries, cancels every resting order that could add exposure, reconciles, lands in
+**SAFE_MODE** — which has no automatic exit and no path back to RUNNING. It does **not**
+close positions, and it keeps what bounds their loss: the orders that only reduce the open
+position (its protective stop, a working exit) stay at the venue. SAFE_MODE does not manage
+the position — no trailing, no break-even, no time stop: the resting stop is its only exit.
+A position left with nothing at the venue is reported unprotected (incident, the
+`unprotected_positions` counter, `last_error`). To get out of the market — or when the stop
+itself is what is wrong — use the flatten below. No model can reach this endpoint or
+override it; the runtime method requires a named human actor.
 
